  "exact_change": "Both nonexistent MessageUtil.toByteBuffer(Message,short) calls become actual MessageUtil.toByteBufferAccessor(Message,short).buffer(). Nothing else changes.",
  "upstream_contract": "Identical official MessageUtil.java lines207-213 in all three releases: one ObjectSerializationCache, message.size(cache,version), exact ByteBuffer.allocate(messageSize), message.write(accessor,cache,version), accessor.flip(), return accessor. Official ByteBufferAccessor.java153-159 flips and exposes same backing buffer. Message.size uses addSize accumulator and Message.write writes all fields for selected version. No version prefix is introduced and no body/header bytes are hand-authored by this correction.",
  "actual_jar_contract": "Actual classfile method descriptors prove toByteBufferAccessor(Message,short)->ByteBufferAccessor and ByteBufferAccessor.buffer()->ByteBuffer are public; no toByteBuffer method is present. Compilation is still pending and not inferred from this source inspection.",
